invariant: INV-19
file: src/quic.c
catches: test/lint-stack-quic.sh
reason: ch_quic_init takes a 4,096-byte scratch buffer, over the 2,560-byte
  budget a device build holds. TRANSPORT=tcp-blocking filters quic.c out of every
  other packaged object, so the plain `make lint-stack` compiles this file
  nowhere and passes; only the TRANSPORT=quic-nonblocking frame-budget check objects.

